  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_soap_cb1ce3462efa7000dd9723ab6a337355dc67f28ffa9a49d456d4bca5495048ba343">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>soap (MED s.v. sope n. (2)) | a wooden case in which soap is packed (OED s.v. soap-box) | ball-soap, commonly used in the North, made with lyes from ashes and tallow (OED s.v. soap 2a, quote 1728) | ashes of certain kinds of wood used in forming a lye in soap-making (OED s.v. soap-ashes) | Castle soape manufactured in Castile, a fine hard soap prepared with olive oil and soda (OED s.v. Castile soap); Venice soape manufactured in Venice | made in Flanders | white soap</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
